# Copy to .env and adjust.
# The AI is normally chosen in Settings, AI (or with `clippy llm <mode>`): ollama, openrouter, claude (your Claude
# subscription), codex (your ChatGPT subscription) or none. That choice wins over the lines below, which are
# the defaults before anyone chose.

# --- 1) Local and free (default): Ollama ---
CLIPPY_LLM_BACKEND=ollama
CLIPPY_LLM_MODEL=clippy-qwen3:14b-q6k
# CLIPPY_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# --- 2) Free hosted APIs (OpenAI-compatible), uncomment one block ---
# Groq (fast, daily quota):
# CLIPPY_LLM_BACKEND=openai
# CLIPPY_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# CLIPPY_LLM_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# CLIPPY_LLM_API_KEY=gsk_...

# Google Gemini (AI Studio key):
# CLIPPY_LLM_BACKEND=openai
# CLIPPY_LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
# CLIPPY_LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# CLIPPY_LLM_API_KEY=...

# OpenRouter (":free" models):
# CLIPPY_LLM_BACKEND=openrouter
# CLIPPY_LLM_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b:free
# CLIPPY_LLM_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# --- LLM tuning (optional) ---
# CLIPPY_LLM_THINK=1          # 1: reasoning mode when picking clips (better choices, slower), 0: fast
# CLIPPY_LLM_CTX=16384        # context in tokens (16K is safe with Q6_K + q8 KV cache on 16 GB VRAM)
# CLIPPY_LLM_KEEP_ALIVE=30m   # how long the model stays loaded in VRAM
# CLIPPY_LLM_CLI_TIMEOUT=600  # seconds the claude and codex modes wait for an answer (a wrong value means 600)

# --- Visual check of reaction peaks (optional, local Ollama only) ---
# A vision model looks at a few frames of the strongest quiet reaction peaks (gameplay, a stream's big moment) and
# tells the clip picker what happens on screen. Off when empty or when the model is not installed
# (ollama pull qwen2.5vl:7b, about 6 GB). Costs one model swap per job, about half a minute to a minute.
# CLIPPY_VISION_MODEL=qwen2.5vl:7b

# --- Other ---
# CLIPPY_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER=firefox   # sites that show a video only when signed in (Instagram, Vimeo, Reddit…)
# CLIPPY_COOKIES_FILE=data/cookies.txt  # or a cookies.txt exported from any signed-in browser (keep it out of git)
# CLIPPY_PORT=7860            # web UI port
# CLIPPY_LAN=1                # phones and tablets on the same Wi-Fi too, after pairing (clippy pair)
# CLIPPY_BROWSER=C:\path\to\browser.exe   # open the UI in this browser instead of Opera GX

# --- Posting to your own channels (docs/publishing.md) ---
# Easier: Settings, Accounts, Set up on each card. These are the same keys, for setups without the app.
# CLIPPY_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com   # Google Cloud, OAuth client of type "Desktop app"
# CLIPPY_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# CLIPPY_TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=...                              # TikTok for Developers, Desktop app
# CLIPPY_TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# CLIPPY_TIKTOK_SCOPES=user.info.basic,video.upload        # without Direct Post (drafts only)
# CLIPPY_INSTAGRAM_APP_ID=...                              # Meta app, API setup with Instagram login
# CLIPPY_INSTAGRAM_APP_SECRET=...

# --- Storage ---
# CLIPPY_LIBRARY=%USERPROFILE%\Videos\Clippy   # finished clips (default: ~/Videos/Clippy)
